From: Lasimeri <217267696+Lasimeri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:20:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] x86/knc: serial AP bring-up on Knights Corner

With parallel bring-up the first SMP boot never completed: the boot CPU
kicks all 227 APs within about 2.5 s and they all contend for the
real-mode trampoline lock with locked read-modify-writes from in-order
cores that have no PAUSE, starving whichever AP holds it (the card was
silent for minutes; test 5, 2026-09-14). With cpuhp.parallel=0 all 228
CPUs come up in about a second (test 8, same day), so parallel mode has
nothing to offer here: the platform layer clears
x86_cpuinit.parallel_bringup, the flag arch_cpuhp_init_parallel_bringup
honours.
---
 arch/x86/kernel/knc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c b/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c
index 6d277aba4..b230ba38f 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/knc.c
@@ -267,6 +267,14 @@ static void __init knc_init_platform(void)
 	 */
 	setup_force_cpu_cap(X86_FEATURE_TSC_RELIABLE);
 
+	/*
+	 * Bring the 227 APs up one at a time: kicked all at once they contend
+	 * for the real-mode trampoline lock with locked read-modify-writes
+	 * from in-order cores without PAUSE, and the first parallel boot never
+	 * completed (test 5, 2026-09-14). Serial bring-up takes about a second.
+	 */
+	x86_cpuinit.parallel_bringup = false;
+
 	machine_ops.emergency_restart		= knc_emergency_restart;
 	pm_power_off				= knc_power_off;
 	atomic_notifier_chain_register(&panic_notifier_list, &knc_panic_nb);
